  "sections": {
   "install": {
    "title": "Get started",
    "html": "<p>You need Python 3.11+, <a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/install/uv.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">uv</a>,\nand a supported AI coding agent on Linux, macOS, or Windows.</p>\n<p>Run these commands in your terminal to install Spec Kit and create a project.\nThis example uses GitHub Copilot.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">uv tool install specify-cli\nspecify init my-project --integration copilot\ncd my-project\n</code></pre>\n<p><a></a></p>\n<p>After installing the Specify CLI and creating your project, launch your coding\nagent in the project directory, then choose a process below.</p>\n<p>For other setups:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/installation.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Installation</a> for pinned releases, other installers, CI, and troubleshooting.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/how-to/existing-projects.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Existing projects</a> to start with code you already have.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/integrations/index.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Other agents</a> for integration keys and <a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/integrations/cli.html#command-invocation\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">invocation syntax</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/upgrade.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Upgrade</a> to update an existing installation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a></a>\n<a></a></p>",
    "truncated": false,
    "chars": 1200
   },
   "usage": null,
   "features": {
    "title": "Capabilities",
    "html": "<p>Spec Kit combines ready-to-use processes with composable mechanisms:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Capability</th>\n<th>Spec Kit mechanism</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Connect to or switch between coding agents</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/integrations/index.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Integration</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Add a command, quality gate, or complete process</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/extensions/overview.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Extension</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Connect a process to an external tool or service</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/extensions/overview.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Extension</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>React to coding-agent lifecycle events</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/extensions/api.html#extension-runtime-events\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Extension runtime event</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Run extension commands before or after Spec Kit commands</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/extensions/api.html#hook-configuration\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Extension hook</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Adapt templates, commands, terminology, or methodology</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/presets/overview.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Preset</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Enforce organizational or regulatory standards</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/presets/overview.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Preset</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Override a template for one project</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/how-to/customization.html#project-local-overrides-and-resolution\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Project-local override</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Automate prompts, commands, gates, and shell tasks</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/workflows/overview.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Workflow</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Modify an installed workflow without forking it</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/workflows/overlays.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Workflow overlay</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Add reusable executable behavior to workflows</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/workflow-steps/developing.html#custom-step-packages\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Workflow step</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Install a curated setup for a role or team</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/bundles/overview.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Bundle</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Discover community components</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/overview/catalogs.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Catalog</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Host a private catalog of approved components</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/overview/catalogs.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Catalog</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Access private catalogs and component downloads</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/reference/authentication.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Authentication</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Work offline or behind a firewall</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/install/air-gapped.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Local sources and self-hosted catalogs</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Inspect which layer supplies a command, template, or script</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.github.io/spec-kit/overview/artifacts.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Artifact inventory</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Search the active catalogs with commands such as <code>specify extension search</code>,\n<code>specify preset search</code>, <code>specify workflow search</code>, and <code>specify bundle search</code>.\nSpec Kit includes community catalogs, and organizations can add their own\ncurated sources. Catalog listings are not audits or endorsements, so review\ncommunity source code before installing or running it.</p>\n<p><a></a>\n<a></a></p>",
